# no-flow oracle, ONE-BYTE map, 64-bit, blob v2 for corrective (x): probe1v2_64_2026-09-19.bin sha256 , 79 forms x 256 = 20224 slots: the 15 v1 forms, then ALL 64 register-form ModRM cells C0..FF with no prefix (a rejected draft pinned rm=000: in the x87 register space rm is opcode). Field held constant here: prefixes (none) on the register-form probes, because the register-form length rule is opcode + ModRM + immediate and no prefix changes the presence of a ModRM; 0x66 on register-form immediates is covered by the v1 66 forms for digit 0 and asserted by the sweep for the rest. ORACLE: Ghidra 12.1.2 PUBLIC, snap revision 47, OpcodeLengths.java restricted to the slot, 0x90 padding.
# PREDICTED before the run: rows 1..3840 identical to the v1 log; register-form cells: x87 D8-DF every defined cell length 2 (D9 C8+i FXCH, DB E3 FNINIT, DB F0+i FCOMI, DD E8+i FUCOMP, D8 C0+i FADD included) and Ghidra NONE on undefined cells (e.g. D9 D1..D7, DB E5..E7: read off, the HAND rule is lenient VALID 2 there); 8F C0..FF: 8F /0 register POP r64 2 and /1-/7 NONE; FF: /0-/6 2, /7 NONE; C6 F8 XABORT 3 and C7 F8 XBEGIN 6 (read off); F6/F7 /0 and /1 register TEST 3 / 6, other digits 2; every other ModRM opcode: length 2 + its digit-0 immediate on all 64 cells, digit-INVALID memory forms notwithstanding (e.g. 8F). Refusals on the refit predicted 0 after the x87 HAND rule; suspects: C6/C7 (register-form digit 7 immediates), 8F.
